ate) through which they were led into Jerusalem","r":"from G4263;","k":"sheep (market).","o":"k84.x.12"},"4263":{"l":"πρόβατον","x":"próbaton","p":"prob'-at-on","d":"something that walks forward (a quadruped), i.e. (specially), a sheep (literally or figuratively)","r":"probably neuter of a presumed derivative of G4260;","k":"sheep(-fold).","o":"i03.1b.1i,i2f.3e.3j,i2n.q.v,i2x.s.x,i4s.26.2b,i4t.u.16,i95.1m.1r,ibf.13.18,ijs.3a.3f,ijt.h.q,il1.3l.3u,iux.32.37,j4d.3k.3t,jqw.z.14,jqy.3k.3p,k59.1d.1i,k5a.2k.2p,kfn.1g.1s,kfo.v.14,kfo.28.2d,kfp.y.13,kfp.1v.24,kfs.27.2j,kft.1m.1v,kfw.1q.1z,kfx.1o.1x,kfx.36.3f,kfx.50.59,kfy.1v.24,kg0.28.2h,kg1.a.f,kgb.19.1e,kgc.3.8,krm.4k.4p,krn.78.7d,kzs.1v.20,lq0.2b.2g,ncl.2q.2v,nh4.f.k,nxa.3d.3i"},"4264":{"l":"προβιβάζω","x":"probibázō","p":"prob-ib-ad'-zo","d":"to force forward, i.e. bring to the front, instigate","r":"from G4253 and a reduplicated form of G971;","k":"draw, before instruct.","o":"i7p.m.w,lb6.9.d"},"4265":{"l":"προβλέπω","x":"problépō","p":"prob-lep'-o","d":"to look out beforehand, i.e. furnish in advance","r":"from G4253 and G991;","k":"provide.","o":"nb8.b.j"},"4266":{"l":"προγίνομαι","x":"progínomai","p":"prog-in'-om-ahee","d":"to be already, i.e. have previousy transpired","r":"from G4253 and G1096;","k":"be past.","o":"lm8.3t.3x"},"4267":{"l":"προγινώσκω","x":"proginṓskō","p":"prog-in-oce'-ko","d":"to know beforehand, i.e. foresee","r":"from G4253 and G1097;","k":"foreknow (ordain), know (before).","o":"lh0.6.a,lpt.g.o,lrn.17.1f,nga.f.r,nkb.x.11,nkb.1f.1l"},"4268":{"l":"πρόγνωσις","x":"prógnōsis","p":"prog'-no-sis","d":"forethought","r":"from G4267;","k":"foreknowledge.","o":"kt8.1g.1t,nfs.n.10"},"4269":{"l":"πρόγονος","x":"prógonos","p":"prog'-on-os","d":"an ancestor, (grand-)parent","r":"from G4266;","k":"forefather, parent.","o":"myv.30.37,n04.y.19"},"4270":{"l":"προγράφω","x":"prográphō","p":"prog-raf'-o","d":"to write previously; figuratively, to announce, prescribe","r":"from G4253 and G1125;","k":"before ordain,